\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Weyl-filtering mechanism and 3D rotational quantum-clutch architecture in true vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$).} \textbf  {a}, Two-dimensional cross-sectional schematic comparing Euclidean parallel plates ($A_{\rm  overlap} > 0$, dominated by attractive proximity-force scaling $F_z^{\rm  PFA} \propto -A_{\rm  overlap}/d^4$), uniform periodic slot-tooth interdigitation ($A_{\rm  overlap} = 0$, limited by single-scale evanescent screening at $\kappa \sim \pi /W_0$), and prefractal Cantor interdigitation ($W_k = W_1 b^{-(k-1)}$, $H_k$, partitioning transverse fringing fields across logarithmically separated wavenumber bands $\kappa _k \sim b^{k-1}\pi /W_1$). \textbf  {b}, Three-dimensional cutaway render of the four-fold symmetric ($C_4$, $90^\circ $ sector period) concentric gold rotor and stator in the disengaged open-slot state ($\theta = 3^\circ $). Downward-protruding concentric rotor teeth ($z \in [-100, 0]\text  { nm}$, $H_1 = 100{}\text  { nm}$, $H_2 = 90{}\text  { nm}$) interdigitate radially inside thin slotted Cantor stator aperture rings ($25\text  { nm}$ membrane thickness, $z \in [-25, 0]\text  { nm}$) suspended above recessed azimuthal landing pads ($150\text  { nm}$ thickness, top surface at $z = -115\text  { nm}$) and supported by a four-spoke $\text  {Si}\langle 110\rangle $ flexure suspension. \textbf  {c},\textbf  {d}, Cutaway renders and axial-radial $(r,z)$ cross-sections in (\textbf  {c}) the disengaged fractal perimeter state ($\theta = 0^\circ \text  {--}6^\circ $, $A_{\rm  overlap} = 0$, $F_z^{\rm  PFA} = 0$, showing upward saddle-point repulsive lift $F_z = +\roundtwo  {3.17743}\text  { pN}$ at $z_{\rm  tip} = -100\text  { nm}$ for $N=3$) and (\textbf  {d}) the engaged Euclidean area state ($\theta = 18^\circ \text  {--}48^\circ $, $A_{\rm  overlap} > 0$ across the $d = 15\text  { nm}$ vertical gap, showing normal attraction $F_z = \roundtwo  {-14.0388}\text  { pN}$ for $N=3$). \textbf  {e}, Radial cross-sectional profiles comparing the single-track baseline ($N=0$), first-generation slot ($N=1$), uniform periodic and monotonic controls, $(r,z)$-scaled $N=2$ Cantor ring, and seven-track $N=3$ Cantor ring across $r \in [0.30, 1.65]\ \mu \text  {m}$.}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rotational_clutch_architecture}{{1}{5}{\textbf {Weyl-filtering mechanism and 3D rotational quantum-clutch architecture in true vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm bg}=1.0$).} \textbf {a}, Two-dimensional cross-sectional schematic comparing Euclidean parallel plates ($A_{\rm overlap} > 0$, dominated by attractive proximity-force scaling $F_z^{\rm PFA} \propto -A_{\rm overlap}/d^4$), uniform periodic slot-tooth interdigitation ($A_{\rm overlap} = 0$, limited by single-scale evanescent screening at $\kappa \sim \pi /W_0$), and prefractal Cantor interdigitation ($W_k = W_1 b^{-(k-1)}$, $H_k$, partitioning transverse fringing fields across logarithmically separated wavenumber bands $\kappa _k \sim b^{k-1}\pi /W_1$). \textbf {b}, Three-dimensional cutaway render of the four-fold symmetric ($C_4$, $90^\circ $ sector period) concentric gold rotor and stator in the disengaged open-slot state ($\theta = 3^\circ $). Downward-protruding concentric rotor teeth ($z \in [-100, 0]\text { nm}$, $H_1 = \CantorNtwoHybridrzHGenoneNm {}\text { nm}$, $H_2 = \CantorNtwoHybridrzHGentwoNm {}\text { nm}$) interdigitate radially inside thin slotted Cantor stator aperture rings ($25\text { nm}$ membrane thickness, $z \in [-25, 0]\text { nm}$) suspended above recessed azimuthal landing pads ($150\text { nm}$ thickness, top surface at $z = -115\text { nm}$) and supported by a four-spoke $\text {Si}\langle 110\rangle $ flexure suspension. \textbf {c},\textbf {d}, Cutaway renders and axial-radial $(r,z)$ cross-sections in (\textbf {c}) the disengaged fractal perimeter state ($\theta = 0^\circ \text {--}6^\circ $, $A_{\rm overlap} = 0$, $F_z^{\rm PFA} = 0$, showing upward saddle-point repulsive lift $F_z = +\roundtwo {\FractalNthreeCantorseventrackBemThetathreeFZPn }\text { pN}$ at $z_{\rm tip} = -100\text { nm}$ for $N=3$) and (\textbf {d}) the engaged Euclidean area state ($\theta = 18^\circ \text {--}48^\circ $, $A_{\rm overlap} > 0$ across the $d = 15\text { nm}$ vertical gap, showing normal attraction $F_z = \roundtwo {\FractalNthreeCantorseventrackBemThetafoureightFZPn }\text { pN}$ for $N=3$). \textbf {e}, Radial cross-sectional profiles comparing the single-track baseline ($N=0$), first-generation slot ($N=1$), uniform periodic and monotonic controls, $(r,z)$-scaled $N=2$ Cantor ring, and seven-track $N=3$ Cantor ring across $r \in [0.30, 1.65]\ \mu \text {m}$}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Multi-scale Cantor force amplification and rotational switching across the six-step verification benchmark in true vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$).} \textbf  {a}, Single-tooth vertical interdigitation ($N=0$) across tooth tip elevation $z_{\rm  tip} \in [-115, -55]\text  { nm}$, showing open-slot repulsive lift ($+\roundtwo  {0.7067}\text  { pN}$ at $z_{\rm  tip} = -100\text  { nm}$) and sign reversal to attraction ($\roundtwo  {-0.359635}\text  { pN}$) under symmetric overhang ($z_{\rm  tip} = -55\text  { nm}$). \textbf  {b}, Unpowered rotational switching ($\theta = 0^\circ $ to $48^\circ $) of axial Casimir force $F_z(\theta )$ (left axis) and normalized landing-pad overlap fraction $A_{\rm  overlap}/A_{\rm  tooth}$ (right axis) across $N=0$ baseline, tight-slot $N=2$ ($C_4$), compact $N=2$ ($C_8$), and seven-track $N=3$ Cantor clutches. \textbf  {c}, Prefractal Cantor generation scaling ($N = 0 \to 3$), reaching $+\roundtwo  {3.17743}\text  { pN}$ open-slot repulsive lift ($4.5{}\times $ over $N=0$) and $\roundtwo  {-14.0388}\text  { pN}$ engaged attraction at $N=3$. \textbf  {d}, Comparison of $N=2$ and $N=3$ Cantor hierarchies against non-fractal controls (single wide tooth, uniform periodic grating, and size-matched monotonic array). \textbf  {e}, Active-tooth-area normalized repulsive force density $F_z/A_{\rm  tooth}$ across the evaluated hierarchies and controls. \textbf  {f}, Active-only versus full-monolithic NEMS structural assemblies incorporating spider spokes, hub collars, and substrate trenches ($<3.3\%$ support crosstalk).}}{6}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:quantum_clutch_architecture_and_narrative}{{2}{6}{\textbf {Multi-scale Cantor force amplification and rotational switching across the six-step verification benchmark in true vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm bg}=1.0$).} \textbf {a}, Single-tooth vertical interdigitation ($N=0$) across tooth tip elevation $z_{\rm tip} \in [-115, -55]\text { nm}$, showing open-slot repulsive lift ($+\roundtwo {\SingletoothTrackzeroBemThetathreeFZPn }\text { pN}$ at $z_{\rm tip} = -100\text { nm}$) and sign reversal to attraction ($\roundtwo {\SingletoothTrackzeroOverhangBemThetathreeFZPn }\text { pN}$) under symmetric overhang ($z_{\rm tip} = -55\text { nm}$). \textbf {b}, Unpowered rotational switching ($\theta = 0^\circ $ to $48^\circ $) of axial Casimir force $F_z(\theta )$ (left axis) and normalized landing-pad overlap fraction $A_{\rm overlap}/A_{\rm tooth}$ (right axis) across $N=0$ baseline, tight-slot $N=2$ ($C_4$), compact $N=2$ ($C_8$), and seven-track $N=3$ Cantor clutches. \textbf {c}, Prefractal Cantor generation scaling ($N = 0 \to 3$), reaching $+\roundtwo {\FractalNthreeCantorseventrackBemThetathreeFZPn }\text { pN}$ open-slot repulsive lift ($\FractalNthreeVsNzeroBemStdRatio {}\times $ over $N=0$) and $\roundtwo {\FractalNthreeCantorseventrackBemThetafoureightFZPn }\text { pN}$ engaged attraction at $N=3$. \textbf {d}, Comparison of $N=2$ and $N=3$ Cantor hierarchies against non-fractal controls (single wide tooth, uniform periodic grating, and size-matched monotonic array). \textbf {e}, Active-tooth-area normalized repulsive force density $F_z/A_{\rm tooth}$ across the evaluated hierarchies and controls. \textbf {f}, Active-only versus full-monolithic NEMS structural assemblies incorporating spider spokes, hub collars, and substrate trenches ($<3.3\%$ support crosstalk)}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Independent three-solver verification and continuum convergence of the rotational quantum clutch in true vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$).} \textbf  {a}, Repulsive-state ($\theta = 3^\circ \text  {--}6^\circ $) surface-mesh refinement across \texttt  {Standard} ($1504{}$ panels), \texttt  {High} ($3120{}$ panels), and \texttt  {Ultra-High} ($6016{}$ panels) discretizations for $N=2$ ($3168{}$ and $6576{}$ panels for $N=3$) in 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM and 3D Scalar-Yukawa BEM. \textbf  {b}, Attractive-state ($\theta = 18^\circ \text  {--}48^\circ $) boundary-element continuum extrapolations ($h = N_{\rm  panels}^{-1/2} \to 0$) compared against 4-pass inclusion--exclusion 3D FDTD MEEP benchmarks and Scalar-Yukawa High-mesh values. \textbf  {c}, Cross-solver comparison (on a symmetric logarithmic scale) across 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM, 3D Scalar-Yukawa BEM, 4-pass 3D FDTD ($R=50$), and 1D Lifshitz--PFA across disengaged repulsive, transition, and engaged attractive rotor angles. \textbf  {d}, Imaginary-frequency Gauss--Legendre quadrature convergence across $n_\xi \in \{16, 24, 32, 40, 64\}$ ($0.00242971{}\%$ drift for $n_\xi \ge 24$, top) and fixed-standoff ($\delta _{\rm  box} = 10{}\text  { nm}$) 4-pass FDTD resolution convergence across $R \in \{40, 50, 60, 80\}$ ($3.1519{}\%$ drift between $R=60$ and $R=80$, bottom).}}{7}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:quantum_clutch_3solver_verification}{{3}{7}{\textbf {Independent three-solver verification and continuum convergence of the rotational quantum clutch in true vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm bg}=1.0$).} \textbf {a}, Repulsive-state ($\theta = 3^\circ \text {--}6^\circ $) surface-mesh refinement across \texttt {Standard} ($\RotCfourTightslotNtwoStandardThetaZerozerosixpzeroPanelCount {}$ panels), \texttt {High} ($\RotCfourTightslotNtwoHighThetaZerozerosixpzeroPanelCount {}$ panels), and \texttt {Ultra-High} ($\RotCfourTightslotNtwoUltraHighThetaZerozerosixpzeroPanelCount {}$ panels) discretizations for $N=2$ ($\RotConezeroFractalNthreeStandardThetaZerozerothreepzeroPanelCount {}$ and $\RotConezeroFractalNthreeHighThetaZerozerothreepzeroPanelCount {}$ panels for $N=3$) in 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM and 3D Scalar-Yukawa BEM. \textbf {b}, Attractive-state ($\theta = 18^\circ \text {--}48^\circ $) boundary-element continuum extrapolations ($h = N_{\rm panels}^{-1/2} \to 0$) compared against 4-pass inclusion--exclusion 3D FDTD MEEP benchmarks and Scalar-Yukawa High-mesh values. \textbf {c}, Cross-solver comparison (on a symmetric logarithmic scale) across 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM, 3D Scalar-Yukawa BEM, 4-pass 3D FDTD ($R=50$), and 1D Lifshitz--PFA across disengaged repulsive, transition, and engaged attractive rotor angles. \textbf {d}, Imaginary-frequency Gauss--Legendre quadrature convergence across $n_\xi \in \{16, 24, 32, 40, 64\}$ ($\BemConvNxiDriftPct {}\%$ drift for $n_\xi \ge 24$, top) and fixed-standoff ($\delta _{\rm box} = \MeepFixedboxMarginNm {}\text { nm}$) 4-pass FDTD resolution convergence across $R \in \{40, 50, 60, 80\}$ ($\MeepFixedboxRsixzeroToReightzeroDriftPct {}\%$ drift between $R=60$ and $R=80$, bottom)}{figure.3}{}}
