\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Spectral wavenumber partitioning and real-space log-periodic stroke oscillations in the 3D Cantor quantum clutch in true vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$).} \textbf  {a}, Normalized 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM radial-wall cross-coupling spectral density $w_m(\kappa )/\max $ and exact signed Casimir force integrand decomposition $\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _{m=1}^{3} \kappa f_{z,m}(\kappa )/\max $ (peak $+\roundtwo  {0.374217}\text  { pN}$, trace decomposition residual $< 10^{-16}\text  { pN}\cdot \mu \text  {m}$) across logarithmic imaginary wavenumber $\ln (\kappa \cdot 1\ \mu \text  {m})$ for the coplanar third-generation seven-track Cantor ring ($N=3$, $b=3$, radial clearances $g_{r,1}=135\text  { nm}$, $g_{r,2}=45\text  { nm}$, $g_{r,3}=15\text  { nm}$; spectral peaks at $\ln \kappa = \roundtwo  {2.70805}, \roundtwo  {3.39883}, \text  {and } \roundtwo  {3.85934}$) compared against the three-track uniform periodic control. Dashed vertical lines mark the inverse radial clearance scales $\kappa = 1/g_{r,m}$. \textbf  {b}, Scale-compensated repulsive lift $|z_{\rm  rotor}|^2 F_z(z_{\rm  rotor})$ swept across $\roundzero  {36}$ logarithmically spaced vertical stroke depths $|z_{\rm  rotor}| \in [25, 450]\text  { nm}$ ($\ln (|z_{\rm  rotor}|/\ell _3) \in [-0.47, 2.42]$) in a three-generation $(r,z)$-self-similar stepped Cantor clutch ($b=2.5{}$, stator stage elevations $|z_{{\rm  stage},m}| \in \{250, 100, 40\}\text  { nm}$) versus a non-geometric three-stage control ($|z_{\rm  stage}| \in \{250, 145, 40\}\text  { nm}$) and a single-scale three-track uniform control ($|z_{\rm  stage}| = 100\text  { nm}$). Dotted vertical lines indicate the logarithmic stage periods $\Delta \ln |z| = \ln b = \roundthree  {0.916291}$. \textbf  {c}, Detrended modulation $\delta (|z|^2 F_z)$ and $95\%$ confidence band extracted via a simultaneous joint quadratic-plus-harmonic least-squares fit to Eq.~\eqref  {eq:fourier_running} at the fixed fundamental scaling frequency $\omega _1 = 2\pi /\ln b = \roundtwo  {6.8572}$ ($R^2 = \roundtwo  {0.529}$, $F = \roundtwo  {7.9214}$, $p = \scinum  {0.00019189}$, $\Delta \mathrm  {AIC} = \roundone  {-18.5828}$, $\Delta \mathrm  {BIC} = \roundone  {-12.2487}$ for the stepped Cantor clutch versus $R^2 = \roundtwo  {0.176312}$, $\Delta \mathrm  {AIC} = +\roundone  {1.35448}$ for the non-geometric 3-stage control and $R^2 = \roundtwo  {0.0141241}$, $\Delta \mathrm  {AIC} = +\roundone  {7.5028}$ for the uniform control).}}{9}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:clutch_log_periodicity}{{4}{9}{\textbf {Spectral wavenumber partitioning and real-space log-periodic stroke oscillations in the 3D Cantor quantum clutch in true vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm bg}=1.0$).} \textbf {a}, Normalized 3D Vector-Dyadic BEM radial-wall cross-coupling spectral density $w_m(\kappa )/\max $ and exact signed Casimir force integrand decomposition $\sum _{m=1}^{3} \kappa f_{z,m}(\kappa )/\max $ (peak $+\roundtwo {\LogperSignedKfTotalPeakPn }\text { pN}$, trace decomposition residual $< 10^{-16}\text { pN}\cdot \mu \text {m}$) across logarithmic imaginary wavenumber $\ln (\kappa \cdot 1\ \mu \text {m})$ for the coplanar third-generation seven-track Cantor ring ($N=3$, $b=3$, radial clearances $g_{r,1}=135\text { nm}$, $g_{r,2}=45\text { nm}$, $g_{r,3}=15\text { nm}$; spectral peaks at $\ln \kappa = \roundtwo {\LogperLnKPeakLone }, \roundtwo {\LogperLnKPeakLtwo }, \text {and } \roundtwo {\LogperLnKPeakLthree }$) compared against the three-track uniform periodic control. Dashed vertical lines mark the inverse radial clearance scales $\kappa = 1/g_{r,m}$. \textbf {b}, Scale-compensated repulsive lift $|z_{\rm rotor}|^2 F_z(z_{\rm rotor})$ swept across $\roundzero {\LogperSteppedRzNZPts }$ logarithmically spaced vertical stroke depths $|z_{\rm rotor}| \in [25, 450]\text { nm}$ ($\ln (|z_{\rm rotor}|/\ell _3) \in [-0.47, 2.42]$) in a three-generation $(r,z)$-self-similar stepped Cantor clutch ($b=\LogperSteppedRzBScale {}$, stator stage elevations $|z_{{\rm stage},m}| \in \{250, 100, 40\}\text { nm}$) versus a non-geometric three-stage control ($|z_{\rm stage}| \in \{250, 145, 40\}\text { nm}$) and a single-scale three-track uniform control ($|z_{\rm stage}| = 100\text { nm}$). Dotted vertical lines indicate the logarithmic stage periods $\Delta \ln |z| = \ln b = \roundthree {\LogperSteppedRzLnB }$. \textbf {c}, Detrended modulation $\delta (|z|^2 F_z)$ and $95\%$ confidence band extracted via a simultaneous joint quadratic-plus-harmonic least-squares fit to Eq.~\eqref {eq:fourier_running} at the fixed fundamental scaling frequency $\omega _1 = 2\pi /\ln b = \roundtwo {\LogperSteppedRzOmegaone }$ ($R^2 = \roundtwo {\LogperSteppedRzRtwo }$, $F = \roundtwo {\LogperSteppedRzFstatCantor }$, $p = \scinum {\LogperSteppedRzPvalCantor }$, $\Delta \mathrm {AIC} = \roundone {\LogperSteppedRzDeltaAicCantor }$, $\Delta \mathrm {BIC} = \roundone {\LogperSteppedRzDeltaBicCantor }$ for the stepped Cantor clutch versus $R^2 = \roundtwo {\LogperSteppedRzRtwoLinear }$, $\Delta \mathrm {AIC} = +\roundone {\LogperSteppedRzDeltaAicLinear }$ for the non-geometric 3-stage control and $R^2 = \roundtwo {\LogperSteppedRzRtwoUniform }$, $\Delta \mathrm {AIC} = +\roundone {\LogperSteppedRzDeltaAicUniform }$ for the uniform control)}{figure.4}{}}
