\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Room-temperature ($T=300{}\text  { K}$) mechanical stability, multi-regime flexure scaling, and quantum readouts in true vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm  bg}=1.0$).} \textbf  {a}, Thermal Matsubara dispersion across ideal PEC ($0\text  { K}$), Drude gold ($0\text  { K}$), and room-temperature Drude gold ($300\text  { K}$) for the $(r,z)$-scaled $N=2$ Cantor ring and compact $N=2$ ($C_8$) variant. \textbf  {b}, Net repulsive restoring force $F_{z,\rm  net}$ across uncompensated root-mean-square electrostatic patch voltages $V_{\rm  rms} \in [0, 80]\text  { mV}$, highlighting the critical zero-force thresholds ($V_{\rm  crit} = \roundone  {90.2392}\text  { mV}$ and $\roundone  {94.1128}\text  { mV}$) and the $<5\text  { mV}$ Kelvin-probe-compensated regime. \textbf  {c}, Destabilizing radial Earnshaw Casimir stiffness $|k_{r,\rm  Casimir}|$ compared on a logarithmic scale against the stabilizing four-spoke single-crystal $\text  {Si}\langle 110\rangle $ radial flexure stiffness $k_{r,\rm  mech}$ ($E_Y = \scinum  {1.69e+11}\text  { Pa}$) across isometric transducer (Regime~I), nanometre-stroke (Regime~II), and contact-release clutch (Regime~III) suspensions. \textbf  {d}, Room-temperature open-slot repulsive lift $F_z(3^\circ )$ and rotational switching swing $\Delta F_z$ across critical-dimension tooth-width etch biases $\Delta w_{\rm  tooth} \in [-10, +10]\text  { nm}$ and EBL corner rounding $r_{\rm  edge} = 5\text  {--}10\text  { nm}$. \textbf  {e}, Atomic cavity QED spectroscopic shifts for hydrogen at the mid-plane ($z = 50\text  { nm}$) of a $d = 100\text  { nm}$ prefractal gap---retarded Casimir--Polder shift $\Delta \nu _{\rm  CP}$, Bethe Lamb shift $\delta \nu _{\rm  Lamb}$, and Lyman-$\alpha $ Purcell modulation $\Delta \Gamma /\Gamma _0$---compared against experimental spectroscopic thresholds. \textbf  {f}, Optomechanical superconducting drum readout showing the log-periodic running Casimir coefficient $C(d_s, \ln (d/\ell _*))/C_0$ and normalized mechanical softening shift $|\Delta \omega _m/\Delta \omega _m^{\rm  flat}|$ across normalized logarithmic gap $\ln (d/\ell _*)$ ($b=3$) relative to the scale-invariant Euclidean baseline ($\partial _{\ln d}C = 0$).}}{11}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:nature_feasibility_stability}{{5}{11}{\textbf {Room-temperature ($T=\NatureRotCeightCompactNtwoCdToleranceTemperatureK {}\text { K}$) mechanical stability, multi-regime flexure scaling, and quantum readouts in true vacuum ($\varepsilon _{\rm bg}=1.0$).} \textbf {a}, Thermal Matsubara dispersion across ideal PEC ($0\text { K}$), Drude gold ($0\text { K}$), and room-temperature Drude gold ($300\text { K}$) for the $(r,z)$-scaled $N=2$ Cantor ring and compact $N=2$ ($C_8$) variant. \textbf {b}, Net repulsive restoring force $F_{z,\rm net}$ across uncompensated root-mean-square electrostatic patch voltages $V_{\rm rms} \in [0, 80]\text { mV}$, highlighting the critical zero-force thresholds ($V_{\rm crit} = \roundone {\NatureCantorNtwoHybridrzPatchPotentialVCritMv }\text { mV}$ and $\roundone {\NatureRotCeightCompactNtwoPatchPotentialVCritMv }\text { mV}$) and the $<5\text { mV}$ Kelvin-probe-compensated regime. \textbf {c}, Destabilizing radial Earnshaw Casimir stiffness $|k_{r,\rm Casimir}|$ compared on a logarithmic scale against the stabilizing four-spoke single-crystal $\text {Si}\langle 110\rangle $ radial flexure stiffness $k_{r,\rm mech}$ ($E_Y = \scinum {\NatureRotCeightCompactNtwoLateralStabilityEYPa }\text { Pa}$) across isometric transducer (Regime~I), nanometre-stroke (Regime~II), and contact-release clutch (Regime~III) suspensions. \textbf {d}, Room-temperature open-slot repulsive lift $F_z(3^\circ )$ and rotational switching swing $\Delta F_z$ across critical-dimension tooth-width etch biases $\Delta w_{\rm tooth} \in [-10, +10]\text { nm}$ and EBL corner rounding $r_{\rm edge} = 5\text {--}10\text { nm}$. \textbf {e}, Atomic cavity QED spectroscopic shifts for hydrogen at the mid-plane ($z = 50\text { nm}$) of a $d = 100\text { nm}$ prefractal gap---retarded Casimir--Polder shift $\Delta \nu _{\rm CP}$, Bethe Lamb shift $\delta \nu _{\rm Lamb}$, and Lyman-$\alpha $ Purcell modulation $\Delta \Gamma /\Gamma _0$---compared against experimental spectroscopic thresholds. \textbf {f}, Optomechanical superconducting drum readout showing the log-periodic running Casimir coefficient $C(d_s, \ln (d/\ell _*))/C_0$ and normalized mechanical softening shift $|\Delta \omega _m/\Delta \omega _m^{\rm flat}|$ across normalized logarithmic gap $\ln (d/\ell _*)$ ($b=3$) relative to the scale-invariant Euclidean baseline ($\partial _{\ln d}C = 0$)}{figure.5}{}}
